 "facts": {
  "policy": {
   "nbp_reference": 3.75,
   "next_mpc_label": "MPC next: 8-9 Apr",
   "pricing_text": "FRAs at the 11 Mar close (1x4 3.80, 3x6 3.82, 6x9 3.87, 9x12 3.90 vs WIBOR 3M 3.80) price roughly 10bp of NBP hikes within 12 months. The MPC cut by 25bp to 3.75% on 4 Mar (a 'hawkish cut', ING); the projection excludes the war. Glapiński (5 Mar): if things calm within about two months, one more cut is back on the table; no forward guidance. Kotecki (11-12 Mar): the March cut was probably the last this year; Janczyk: wait-and-see for months.",
   "risk_text": "Oil and the war set the direction: if Brent stays near $100 the market keeps pricing NBP hikes and the front-end roll-down reverses; a ceasefire would bring cuts back (Glapiński's 'two months'). SAFE politics add a fiscal premium."
  },
  "macro": {
   "cpi": {
    "v": 2.2,
    "m": "Jan flash (GUS, 13 Feb; old weights)"
   },
   "projection_text": "NBP March projection (4 Mar; data to 19 Feb, war excluded): CPI 50% bands 1.6-2.9% (2026), 1.1-3.7% (2027); central path 2.3% / 2.4% / 2.3% (2026-28), GDP 3.9% in 2026 (Inflation Report, 6 Mar).",
   "fiscal_text": "2025 general-government deficit ~7.0% of GDP (MoF figures in Fitch: 7.0% / 6.5% / 6.2% for 2025-27, debt ~70% of GDP by 2027); 2026 deficit cap PLN 271.7bn.",
   "fiscal_risk_text": "2026 needs ~38% (25 Feb) financed; MoF cancelled the 11 Mar switch; budget accounts ~PLN 171.6bn at end-February. Moody's reviews Poland on 20 Mar (A2, negative).",
   "backdrop_text": "The NBP cut to 3.75% on 4 Mar after holding at 4.00% in January and February; January flash CPI 2.2%; 2025 GDP 3.6%, Q4 4.0%. Ratings: Fitch A- negative (affirmed 27 Feb), Moody's A2 negative, S&P A- stable. 11 Mar: Kotecki said the March cut was 'rather the end' for this year; short POLGB yields jumped up to 21bp; BGK cancelled its 12 Mar FPC auction; Glapiński announced active management of NBP gold. Abroad: US February CPI in line (core 2.5% y/y); the IEA announced a record 400m-barrel release; ECB's Kazimir said a hike may be closer than many think."
  },
  "calendar": {
   "plan_text": "MoF March plan (27 Feb): sale auctions on 18 and 25 Mar (PLN 7-13bn each; OK0128, NZ0331, PS0731 (new 5Y fixed), DS1035, NZ0936 (new 10Y POLSTR floater)) and a switch on 11 Mar buying back OK0426, DS0726, PS1026, WZ1126 and OK0127; no T-bills; WZ sales ended in February. February sales were ~PLN 41bn; ~38% of 2026 needs financed. 9 Mar: MoF cancelled the 11 Mar switch because of market volatility. BGK cancelled its 12 Mar FPC auction (11 Mar).",
   "timing_text": "The Aug 2025-Feb 2026 pattern (auction-day close the cheapest point of the week) comes from a rally regime; in March's sell-off MoF is cutting supply (switch instead of sale, a smaller 25 Mar offer), so remaining dates (18 and 25 Mar) are less of a supply event. Next MPC 8-9 Apr: a hold is expected while the market prices hikes.",
